Ah thankyou for the reference and thanks for pushing a fix so quickly i knew there was something @nicolasva i did check the source of tmpdir, but overlooked due to last change date opps..

i will note i have currently worked around the issue in our environments by using EBS storage for the pods via https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/ephemeral-volumes/#generic-ephemeral-volumes the cost isnt huge ~10 cents per pod but ideally id prefer to reduce this complexity and cost. 

@nicolasva OOC, How does rails 8.1.2 cause it to use 3.4 tmpdir even though we have been running 3.4 for a while, rather how does that magic occur?

@byroot @yahonda May I resolve this issue?
I just want to know if this issue is open for contribution. Looking forward to your response.

Regards

@byroot Thanks for clarifying that errors in `rescue_responses` aren't intended to be reported by the error reporter! There's still the odd behavior that if `enable_reloading` is true, those errors *do* get reported. Is that intentional? It seems like it could lead to confusing differences between development and production like the one that caused this issue to be opened.

With a little more digging, I determined that setting `enable_reloading` to true but then removing the `ActionDispatch::Reloader` middleware stopped the errors from being reported, so it seems like it's something about that middleware that's causing the `rescue_responses` errors to be reported. And looking at the code, that makes some sense: `ActionDispatch::ShowExceptions` is in the default middleware stack between the standard `ActionDispatch::Executor` and the reloader, so ShowExceptions can only affect the following code when it's being run in the context of the standard executor and not in the context of the reloader:

https://github.com/rails/rails/blob/a3b37ff166a925f7e069c9068f7ee92808da6e82/actionpack/lib/action_dispatch/middleware/executor.rb#L15-L29

So you override `on_rotation` when it's defined with the second `rotate`. For example:
```ruby
Post.signed_id_verifier.rotate "old_secret", on_rotation: -> { puts "This is not called!" }
Post.signed_id_verifier.rotate "old_secret2", on_rotation: -> { puts "This is called!" }
```
Did I understand it correctly?

@byroot Thanks for the fix!
Another point, do you think this test should be added for Signed Id -> [PR#54362](https://github.com/rails/rails/pull/54362)
or it's already tested for MessageVerifier and this is not needed?
